 "result": "squeeze.py is a stdlib-only wrapper around lzma. Mode c compresses stdin with FORMAT_ALONE at preset 9|EXTREME, and mode d decompresses it, so the round trip is lossless by construction. The assay was accepted with baseline 5.4748 and noise 0.0%, and every output was correct. One variant (LZMA2 raw with lc=4, lp=0, pb=0, dict 16 MiB) scored 5.498, about +0.4%, which is below the 3% win threshold, so the incumbent was kept. I am resting rather than spending more energy, because further gains from parameter tuning look marginal.",
